{"tool_name":"scadie","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scadie","home":"https://github.com/tdw1221/SCADIE","license":"MIT","summary":"Aimultaneous estimation of cell type proportions and cell type-specific gene expressions using SCAD-based iterative estimating procedure.","addition_date":"2022-09-02T23:41:39.779555Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:43:55.648987Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scadie","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"hongyu.zhao@yale.edu","name":"Hongyu Zhao","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1195-9607","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Daiwei Tang"},{"name":"Seyoung Park"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Differential gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"}]}],"name":"SCADIE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-022-02688-w","metadata":{"abstract":"A challenge in bulk gene differential expression analysis is to differentiate changes due to cell type-specific gene expression and cell type proportions. SCADIE is an iterative algorithm that simultaneously estimates cell type-specific gene expression profiles and cell type proportions, and performs cell type-specific differential expression analysis at the group level. Through its unique penalty and objective function, SCADIE more accurately identifies cell type-specific differentially expressed genes than existing methods, including those that may be missed from single cell RNA-Seq data. SCADIE has robust performance with respect to the choice of deconvolution methods and the sources and quality of input data.","authors":[{"name":"Park S."},{"name":"Tang D."},{"name":"Zhao H."}],"citationCount":4,"d